# Component repositories — cloned by ./bootstrap.sh as INDEPENDENT git checkouts.
# They are not tracked by this meta-repo (each has its own github.com/yegamble/<name> repo).
/vidra-core/
/vidra-user/
/vidra-search/

# Ralph runtime/generated files (root .ralph/ is kept for its product specs/docs)
**/.ralph/.call_count
**/.ralph/.last_reset
**/.ralph/.last_output_length
**/.ralph/.loop_start_sha
**/.ralph/.token_count
**/.ralph/.exit_signals
**/.ralph/status.json
**/.ralph/progress.json
**/.ralph/live.log
**/.ralph/.ralph_session
**/.ralph/.ralph_session_history
**/.ralph/.claude_session_id
**/.ralph/.response_analysis
**/.ralph/.circuit_breaker_state
**/.ralph/.circuit_breaker_history
**/.ralph/logs/*
!**/.ralph/logs/.gitkeep
**/.ralph/docs/generated/*
!**/.ralph/docs/generated/.gitkeep
.ralph_backup_*

# Filled-in environment files. `deploy/README.md` tells the operator to
# `cp env/production.env.example env/production.env` and then paste real
# secrets (JWT_SECRET, POSTGRES_PASSWORD, the envelope KEKs) into it, so the
# concrete *.env files must never be committable. Only the *.example templates
# — which carry placeholders and generation recipes — stay tracked.
env/*.env
!env/*.env.example
# ...and their backups. `deploy/rollback.sh` does `cp "$ENV_FILE" "$ENV_FILE.bak"`
# before it rewrites the image tags, producing `env/production.env.bak` — a
# byte-for-byte copy of every production secret that the `env/*.env` glob above
# does NOT match (the name does not end in `.env`). Listed after the
# `.env.example` negation so the ordering is explicit; `.env.example` files are
# unaffected because they do not end in `.env.bak`.
env/*.env.bak
# ...and the setup engine's atomic-write temp files. `vidra setup` writes an env
# file through `os.CreateTemp(dir, "."+base+".tmp*")` + rename (vidra-core
# internal/setup/setup.go), i.e. `env/.production.env.tmpNNNNN`. A crash between
# create and rename leaves that file behind holding every generated secret, and
# neither `env/*.env` nor the global `*.tmp` rule above matches the name (the
# random suffix comes AFTER `.tmp`). Ignore the shape, not one instance.
env/.*.tmp*

# The GENERATED reverse-proxy config. `vidra setup` renders
# deploy/Caddyfile.local from the committed deploy/Caddyfile template plus the
# env file, and docker-compose.prod.yml mounts ONLY the .local file. It carries
# the operator's real domain and ACME contact address, and every host's copy
# differs, so it is deliberately not committable — the template is what this
# repo ships and reviews.
deploy/Caddyfile.local
# The OTHER generated proxy config: `vidra setup --tls-mode external` writes
# deploy/nginx-external.conf.example as a starting point for the nginx/HAProxy
# the operator runs themselves. Same reasoning as the Caddyfile — it is rendered
# from their env file, not shipped by this repo — but it also has a mechanical
# consequence if left untracked. install.sh decides whether to fast-forward a
# git-mode tree with a pathspec-less `git status --porcelain`, so ONE untracked
# generated file there means "has uncommitted changes, nothing was fetched" on
# every future run: the tree would never update again.
deploy/nginx-external.conf.example
# ...and the same atomic-write temp files the env rule above covers. The setup
# engine renders the Caddyfile through `os.CreateTemp(dir, "."+base+".tmp*")` +
# rename, i.e. `deploy/.Caddyfile.local.tmpNNNNN`. A crash between create and
# rename leaves it behind, and neither `deploy/Caddyfile.local` nor the global
# `*.tmp` rule below matches (the random suffix comes AFTER `.tmp`). This is the
# deploy/ half of `env/.*.tmp*` — env/ had both patterns, deploy/ only the first.
deploy/.*.tmp*

# The no-git deployment bundle: deploy/make-bundle.sh's output, and the marker
# file it puts at the root of the tree it produces.
#
# `vidra-bundle.manifest` is ignored because its PRESENCE IS A STATEMENT: it is
# how deploy.sh and rollback.sh tell an unpacked bundle from a git checkout, and
# they behave differently for each (a bundle has no component checkouts to sync
# and no migrations directory to read the expected schema version from). A
# manifest committed to this repository would make every clone claim to be a
# bundle, and the two would be indistinguishable exactly where it matters.
vidra-bundle.manifest
vidra-bundle_*.tar.gz
/dist/

# Local backup artifacts written by deploy/backup.sh and deploy/deploy.sh.
# These are full pg_dumps: they contain every user row and every secret the
# application persists, so they are never allowed near git.
/backups/

# Logs / OS / temp
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.tmp
.temp/

# IDE files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.gstack/
.playwright-mcp/

# Stray package-manager artifacts from ad-hoc npx/pnpm-dlx runs (no JS package at the meta-repo root)
/node_modules/
/.pnpm-store/

# Claude Code: share the council agents, keep local state out
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/hooks/.state/
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/worktrees/
